s, who cites Philolaus as having written that God had","Origin of Discoveries Attributed to the Moderns"],[0,0,-1,1622,"69c7faaf6c6f3cc53c842b61",1022,"Not only the Fathers or Christian theologians, but also ethnic philosophers, removed all use of the sensitive part entirely from the separated soul, specifically Plotinus in the fourth Ennead , book 4, chapter 23, and Philolaus the Pythagor","Theologia naturalis. Sive entis increati et creati"],[0,0,-1,470,"69942bf5b2f6748db4abc741",174,"Now I return to Philolaus, from whom I have digressed by a great interval, who in the third of the volumes which he entitles Peri rhythmōn kai metrōn , speaks thus concerning the human soul: \"The soul is placed into the body 15 through numb","The Works of Claudianus Mamertus"],[0,0,-1,1873,"6955770857e3b773024f2e57",581,"In the fragment of Philolaus, analyzed by Claudius Mamertus, De Statu Animae , II, 3, we see the relationship of the soul to the harmonious constitution of the universe.","Pythagoras and Pythagorean Philosophy"],[0,0,-1,1819,"699058fdaaa7f10ed4cfa811",33,"\" For the remaining third book, a reference to Philolaus \"in the [work] On the Soul \" in the writings of Stobaeus 1) presents itself quite opportunely: and that the third book really did deal with the soul, I confirm from Claudianus Mamertu","Philolaos des Pythagoreers Lehren nebst den Bruchstücken seines Werkes"],[0,0,-1,1819,"699058fdaaa7f10ed4cfa811",38,"n form no other idea of it than that Claudianus Mamertus had a collection of musical or arithmetic matters before him, whether the heading read of rhythms or of numbers ; 1) among these, the books of Philolaus might have been located becaus","Philolaos des Pythagoreers Lehren nebst den Bruchstücken seines Werkes"],[0,0,-1,1819,"699058fdaaa7f10ed4cfa811",182,"From Claudianus Mamertus (On the State of the Soul II, 7), one can conclude that Philolaus was quite detailed regarding the life and weaving of the world soul, as well as the relationship of individual souls to it; and one may expect that h","Philolaos des Pythagoreers Lehren nebst den Bruchstücken seines Werkes"],[0,0,-1,1881,"6a3f02bb97e91e1768f68204",75,"Indeed, Claudianus Mamertus, in book 2, chapter 7, makes Philolaus speak in this way: \"The soul is composed according to the example of the unit, which rules in the body without location, just as the unit rules in numbers.","Fragments of Greek Philosophers"],[0,0,-1,1733,"697a80bce680cef7cedae39d",424,"CLAUDIANUS MAMERTUS (z) indicates that PHILOLAUS , the Pythagorean, held the same opinion.","Volume of Dissertations on Ecclesiastical History"]],"nodes":[[3,-1,0],[2,-1,0],[9,-1,0],[0,-1,0],[1,-1,0],[5,-1,0],[6,-1,0],[7,-1,0],[4,-1,0],[8,-1,0]]}]}